## Exclusions, era, margins, gaps

**Excluded (2 of 5):** p218 Pinault and p219 Graves, both `crossing_undatable`. Private/early timber and private restaurant chains did not publish a below-bar/above-bar pair inside 10 years. That is the intended outcome.

**Pre-1995 hit:** **1 definite** (p217 Knight, 1970–1972). p220 Garcia’s bound is 1992–1995 and **straddles 1995** (midpoint 1993.5). Chesky is post-1995. The two excluded rows have no dated hit.

**Margin under 20% above the bar:** none of the dated above-bar figures. Knight’s *below-bar* 1969 Britannica $1M is 12% short of that year’s bar — flagged in notes; it does not move the bound.

**Blunt gaps:** Pinault and Graves a5 really are undatable from published revenue. Garcia and Pinault a2 are unknown after two attempts. Chesky’s crossing year inside 2008–2015 is not in any filing I reached. I did not stretch a 10-year window to save any of those rows.

